// Title: Powershell Executed From Headless ConHost Process
// Sigma ID: 056c7317-9a09-4bd4-9067-d051312752ea
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Matt Anderson (Huntress)
// Date: 2024-07-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059.001, T1059.003, T1564.003
// Description: Detects the use of powershell commands from headless ConHost window. The "--headless" flag hides
//   the windows from the user upon execution.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/fake-browser-updates-lead-to-boinc-volunteer-computing-software
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_conhost_headless_powershell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\conhost.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CONHOST.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--headless" and ProcessCommandLine contains "powershell")
